Given an array arr[] consisting of n integers, find all the array elements which occurs more than floor(n/3) times. Return the resulting array in strictly increasing order. If no such elements exist, return an empty array.

Examples:
Input: arr[] = [2, 2, 3, 1, 3, 2, 1, 1]
Output: [1, 2]
Explanation: The frequency of 1 and 2 is 3, which is more than floor n/3 (8/3 = 2).
*******************************************************SOLUTION************************************************************

class Solution {
    public ArrayList<Integer> findMajority(int[] arr) {
        int size = arr.length;
        int Maxfreq = size / 3;
        ArrayList<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();
        
        if(size == 0) return result;
        
        Arrays.sort(arr);
        int count = 1;
        for(int i = 1; i < size; i++){
            if(arr[i] == arr[i-1]){
                count++;
            }
            else{
                if (count > Maxfreq){
                    result.add(arr[i-1]);
                }
                count = 1;
            }
        }
        
        if(count > Maxfreq){
            result.add(arr[size-1]);
        }
        return result;
    }
}
